      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation separates dense encoding from window partitioning, and the partition operates on the field rather than replacing it.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into a dense feature field. That field is the persistent carrier read and updated by the compact process. Window partitioning forms tokens from the carrier while keeping the dense field as the source.",
